check 1
# Client state of combat-melee-fallen: the 1.14d client unit sets (traces/pc1/client-state/combat-melee-fallen.cstate.jsonl, state-snapshot.md section 3 rule 5) against the ClientWorld of d2-client (state-dump --client-out); same save, seed, pokes and input as combat-melee-fallen.
# Melee on a poked fallen from one shared input script: a level-3
# Barbarian with a short sword (right hand) warped to the Blood Moor
# (level 2) before frame 4; before frame 30 the game seed and the player's
# unit seed are fixed and a fallen party (monstats 19, normal) is spawned
# 3 sub-tiles east of the player; `clickunit 1 19` at frame 39: the
# cursor on the nearest fallen's drawn point before frame 39's drain, the
# left click before frame 40's (the hover frame: 1.14d picks the hovered
# unit while drawing; autostart.py's `nearest` on 1.14d, the d2rs model
# camera on d2rs; scenario-diff.md §2 rule 4.5). The click sends the
# attack on the unit (C->S 0x06 [type 1][GUID]; ui/controls.md §6 r8),
# not a walk. Compare the player's mode and the party's hp / mode frame
# by frame (state; the party's GUIDs differ: 19-21 on 1.14d, 17-19 on
# d2rs), and the C->S ids (packets: d2rs only until record_packets.py
# applies framed input).
# Spec: specs/tools/scenario-diff.md.
name cs-combat-melee-fallen
save CmbBar --class bar --expansion --level 3 --item ssd/body=4
seed 1234
ticks 150
seconds 300
channels cstate
at 4 poke warp 2
at 30 poke seed-game 0x00001234 666
at 30 poke seed-unit @player 0x00000055 666
at 30 poke spawn 19 @x+3 @y normal
input frame 39; clickunit 1 19
